add('p0','这一步要回答：三块砖 A=[0,0,1,2]、B=[1,0,2,1]、C=[1,1,2,2]，能恰好铺满 2×2 正方形吗？[x,y,a,b] 表示左下角 (x,y)、右上角 (a,b)，边平行于坐标轴。恰好覆盖指内部每一点都被覆盖一次；边或角相接是允许的。','Can A=[0,0,1,2], B=[1,0,2,1], and C=[1,1,2,2] exactly tile a 2×2 square? In [x,y,a,b], (x,y) is the bottom-left corner and (a,b) the top-right; edges follow the coordinate axes. Exact cover means every interior point is covered once. Shared edges and corners are allowed.')
add('rules','官方范围：砖数 n 满足 1 ≤ n ≤ 20,000；坐标为 −100,000 到 100,000 的整数，x<a 且 y<b，所以每块砖面积为正。返回布尔值，不要求修改输入。','Official limits: tile count n satisfies 1 ≤ n ≤ 20,000; integer coordinates from −100,000 to 100,000, with x<a and y<b, so every tile has positive area. Return a boolean; input mutation is not required.')
add('handTask','横轴 x 向右，纵轴 y 向上；每个数字是该单位小格被覆盖的次数。先检查四格，再心算 (1−0)×(2−0) + 1×1 + 1×1，最后揭晓。图是教学模拟；窄屏可横向滚动。','The x-axis points right and y points up. Each number counts how many tiles cover that unit cell. Inspect all four cells, then calculate (1−0)×(2−0) + 1×1 + 1×1 before revealing. This is a teaching simulation; scroll horizontally on narrow screens.')
add('handShow','揭晓手算','Reveal hand calculation')
add('handHide','收起手算','Hide hand calculation')
add('handAnswer','A 面积 2，B 面积 1，C 面积 1，总面积 4。左边两格只属于 A，右下格只属于 B，右上格只属于 C，因此每格都是 1，答案 true。仅仅算出 4 还不够，下一步看为什么。','A has area 2, B area 1, and C area 1: total 4. The two left cells belong only to A; the bottom-right to B and top-right to C. Every count is 1, so the answer is true. Getting a total of 4 alone is insufficient; next we will see why.')
add('p1','这一步要回答：总面积等于外框面积，为什么还可能失败？外框（包围盒）是所有砖的最小外接矩形，由最小 x、y 和最大 a、b 决定。面积是宽×高，以平方单位计。','Why can equal total area still fail? The bounding box is the smallest rectangle enclosing all tiles, given by the smallest x and y and largest a and b. Area is width times height, in square units.')
add('baselineText','先用独立的笨办法：对外框内每个整数单位格，扫描所有砖，要求覆盖次数（盖住该格的砖数）恰为 1。整数边界保证单位格内部不会再被切开，所以这能正确判断。手算的三块砖仍得到四个 1。','Start with an independent baseline: for every integer unit cell in the box, scan all tiles and require its coverage count (the number covering it) to be exactly 1. Integer boundaries cannot split a unit-cell interior, so this test is correct. Our three tiles still produce four ones.')
add('baselineCost','设外框宽 W、高 H，共 WH 个单位格，基线需要 O(nWH) 时间、O(1) 额外空间。最大外框有 40,000,000,000 格；即使先分割成不同坐标之间的格子，也可能有 O(n²) 格。我们需要绕开逐格访问。','For box width W and height H there are WH unit cells. This baseline takes O(nWH) time and O(1) auxiliary space. The largest box has 40,000,000,000 cells. Even splitting only at distinct input coordinates can create O(n²) cells. We need to avoid visiting each cell.')
add('wrong','反例：两份 [0,0,1,2] 加上 [2,0,3,2]。外框是 3×2，面积和 2+2+2=6 也等于 6；但每行覆盖次数为 2、0、1。左边重叠恰好抵消中间空洞。可在下一步选择“面积陷阱”亲自检查。','Counterexample: two copies of [0,0,1,2] plus [2,0,3,2]. The box is 3×2 and total area 2+2+2=6 matches it, but each row has counts 2,0,1. The left overlap balances the middle gap. Select “Area trap” in the next step to inspect it.')
add('p2','这一步要回答：不走遍小格，能保留什么证据？还是从三块砖开始。奇数角点集合只保存出现次数为奇数的坐标；切换一个角点，就是不存在时加入、已存在时删除。这种只关心奇偶的记录叫奇偶性。','What evidence can we keep without visiting every cell? Return to the three tiles. The odd corner set stores coordinates seen an odd number of times. Toggling a corner means adding it if absent and removing it if present. Tracking only odd versus even is called parity.')
add('derive','处理 A 后四个角都在集合中，面积 2。处理 B 时 (1,0) 第二次出现而删除；(1,1)、(2,0)、(2,1) 首次出现而加入，面积变成 3。处理 C 时 (1,1)、(1,2)、(2,1) 都删除，只加入 (2,2)，面积变成 4。最终只剩外框四角。T 形接缝处 (1,1) 虽然有三块砖相邻，却只有 B、C 把它当角点，所以也抵消。','After A, its four corners remain and area is 2. B removes (1,0) on its second occurrence and adds (1,1), (2,0), (2,1); area becomes 3. C removes (1,1), (1,2), (2,1) and adds only (2,2); area becomes 4. Only the box corners remain. At the T-junction (1,1), three tiles meet, but only B and C have a corner there, so it cancels too.')
add('invariant','不变量（每处理完一块砖都成立的事实）：area 是已处理砖的面积和，corners 恰是已处理角点出现奇数次的坐标集合，外框由已处理砖的最小/最大坐标给出。每块砖加一次面积、切换四次角点，直接保持这三个事实。最终必须同时满足：area 等于外框面积，corners 恰等于外框四角。','Invariant (a fact true after every processed tile): area is the processed tiles’ area sum; corners contains exactly their odd-occurrence corner coordinates; the current box uses their minimum/maximum coordinates. Adding each tile’s area and toggling its four corners preserves all three facts. At the end, require both area equal to box area and corners equal to the four box corners.')
add('traceTask','先保持“三块拼接”，逐次添加砖：看图中覆盖次数、下方四次切换及集合的前后变化。再换“面积陷阱”和“三重覆盖”，到终点比较两项检查。换预设会从 0 块重新开始；只影响本实验。','Keep “Three-tile cover” and add tiles one at a time. Watch cell counts, the four toggles, and the before/after corner sets. Then try “Area trap” and “Triple coverage” and compare both final checks. Changing the preset restarts this experiment at zero tiles; other exercises are independent.')
add('simulation','此图用 JavaScript 模拟已完成的整块更新，不执行下方 Python。所有帧完整保留，无省略。图的虚线是完整预设的外框；读数中的外框仅属于已处理前缀（从第一块到当前块）。','This JavaScript diagram simulates completed whole-tile updates; it does not execute the Python below. Every frame is retained with no omissions. The dashed diagram box encloses the full preset; the readout box encloses only the processed prefix (the first tile through the current one).')
add('marking','数字 0=空洞，1=单层，≥2=重叠；带坐标的圆点=当前奇数角点。横轴 x 向右，纵轴 y 向上。配色仅辅助，数字与坐标才是数据。窄屏可横向滚动图表。','Numbers: 0=gap, 1=single layer, ≥2=overlap. Labeled dots mark current odd corners. x increases rightward and y upward. Color assists; numbers and coordinates carry the data. Scroll the diagram horizontally on narrow screens.')
